Z||000000||Songman||05-23-2001||08:44 PM||||Can anyone tell me what they use to do this with? I have created videos in the past for websites but always streamed them using RealVideo. The quality on these is really poor.<P>Some of these Fiero videos I have seen on here are pretty high quality, but still stream fairly fast.<P>Any help would be appreciated. I am going from a VCR into my WinTV video card as my source.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||05-23-2001||09:27 PM||||Your best bet would be asf.. it allows streaming(asx)or downloading of the video(asf).. <BR>more info can be found at <A HREF="http://www.vcdhelp.com" TARGET=_blank>www.vcdhelp.com</A>    and if you need any of the programs needed to do these, pm me.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroSTETZ||05-24-2001||03:08 AM||||go to <A HREF="http://www.shawnrocks.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shawnrocks.com</A>  - that is my page, there are mpeg 1, 2, and wmv files, it gives a good comparison of all of them. to use wmv (notice that files only a meg!) you can use windows media encoder, at microsoft.com<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/view6.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.shawnrocks.com/SHAWN.GIF"> ||||reg||1
